From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:54:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(control): send settings as key and value, not as a config
 line

The translator was formatting `key = "value"` because the entry point took a
config-file line, so every value had to survive that file's syntax on the way
out. It didn't: WT's default wordDelimiters contains a backslash and a double
quote, the value lost its meaning to the quoting, and ghostty rejected it
through a diagnostic that libghostty built without an app runtime never
surfaces. The setting looked forwarded while ghostty kept its own word
boundaries - visible only as a double click keeping a trailing "." that
cascadia dropped.

ghostty_config_set_kv takes the key and the value separately and parses
neither, so the quoting and the escaping here go away entirely and values
reach the engine as the profile holds them.

One escaping rule survives, and it belongs somewhere else: selection-word-chars
is parsed as a Zig string literal by the *field*, so a lone backslash starts an
escape sequence there and WT's delimiters contain one that is not valid. That
is this key's own syntax, not the entry's, and the comment and the test now say
so. Nothing else is touched, backslashes and quotes included.

Covered by the symptom rather than by the shape: scripts/smoke-harness.ps1
feeds "Microsoft Corporation. Ltd" into the real engine with WT's delimiters
and requires a double click to come back "Corporation".

WT suites: terminalCore 54/54, unitSettingsModel 159/159, unitControl 54/54,
terminalApp 51/51.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgDGqEqRBB8L5Ueoq1uuxy
